        "body": "<p>We value the expression of the material itself—and the breath of the maker—more than loud finishing or fashion.</p><p>The aroma of tea leaves, the glaze on a bowl, the weave of an obi: the more we leave untouched, the more a character that can only be born in that place comes forward.</p><p>No two are the same.</p><p>That is why every encounter is once in a lifetime. Do not miss the feeling in your hands.</p>",
